:1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Note:** I can't see the bank's iShares example. The US points reflect typical practice, so check them against the fund's prospectus and SAI.\n\n**Risks and controls**\n- **Borrower default:** Securities aren't returned. Controls: counterparty credit limits, borrower diversification, agent indemnification where contracted.\n- **Collateral shortfall:** After a default, liquidated collateral may not cover repurchase cost (market gaps, wrong-way risk). Controls: over-collateralisation, daily mark-to-market, margin calls, haircuts, concentration limits.\n- **Cash reinvestment:** Reinvested cash can lose value or become illiquid, usually at the fund's expense. Controls: conservative money-market vehicles, maturity and credit limits.\n\n**US (1940 Act):** Collateral is typically ≥102% (domestic) or 105% (international). Lending is capped at one-third of assets.\n\n**UCITS (ESMA/2014/937):**\n- Securities recallable at any time.\n- Collateral liquid, high-quality, diversified (~20% per issuer), valued daily and haircut.\n- No reuse of non-cash collateral.\n- Cash reinvested only in deposits, high-quality government bonds, reverse repos or short-term MMFs.\n\nCollateral mitigates losses but doesn't eliminate them.","ttft_ms":5208,"type":"result","duration_ms":8157,"uuid":"8f3a107e-e8f1-446c-a22a-127503ae4e99","ttft_stream_ms":1174,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1175,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
